        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-09T03:32:39.091Z",
          "text": "show states where something has been noted in the document but not integrated yet (dotted lines)",
          "edited": "2026-11-09T03:33:17.511Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T03:33:49.917Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  every row of Item states shows its chip.</p><p>The table was also out of date, so I rewrote it from the code:  it now has every state in the order they're decided, including the ones P63 added.</p>",
          "commit": "418f039cd"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-09T03:41:46.987Z",
          "text": "show them in the colors they actually display, with e.g. `T1`.\nAlso show the dotted appearance when I've commented but not submitted yet",
          "edited": "2026-11-09T03:42:34.160Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T04:02:41.465Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  each row now shows the chip as an epic page draws it, with an id like <code>T1</code>.  A chip that's outlined or dotted on a page is outlined or dotted here.</p><p>A new table under it shows a chip while your answer is on its way:  dotted blue once you've marked it, until Claude takes the mark in.</p><p>One gap:  a comment, or a note you've typed and not sent, doesn't turn the chip dotted today.  I've asked you whether it should.</p>",
          "commit": "4a553b0"
        }
      ],
